  "sceneDirections": [
    {
      "sourceLine": 3,
      "title": "The page arrives",
      "direction": "Thursday five, Kiva awake with right-hand blisters. Page headed by Penhale reaches every catcher. It names a sheet and teaches the sleeve lesson without rewriting its title. Ink and work carry the loss."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 33,
      "title": "Ivey returns the sheets",
      "direction": "Two copies, for Yeo and Ivey. Kiva agrees to teach in the yard on a non-Lane evening. Pike taught the second’s sheet. No new contract or seat."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 53,
      "title": "The week’s crossing and the hurt four",
      "direction": "Thursday seven. Four warm mornings permit a seventh crossing but do not require it. Forecast past elbow, five nights perhaps six; weekly calendar makes Wednesday unavailable if spent now. Kiva keeps it for Wednesday without knowing thirty-six hands or being asked. Perrin supports choice. His rib lift restarts fortnight from Wednesday; Jude right edge only, no left grip till Monday; Pru may catch but must not grip poles."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 159,
      "title": "Anwen teaches Lyle",
      "direction": "Reset to Anwen at eight. Treen calls Set, Carrow lights only edge on another’s word. Lyle learns lean through stance from floor instead of absent wall. Anwen teaches an opponent because she promised; warmth and wry daft remain restrained. No power restoration."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 235,
      "title": "Draw and draft",
      "direction": "Reset to Kiva at 9:45 reading Thursday draw posted last night. Seven faces Tarn second, not injured first. Draft card is not seat. Jude touches and leaves his card; Perrin avoids his two. Preserve unresolved choices."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 265,
      "title": "The Lane",
      "direction": "Seven declares Pryce ward, Talley edge, Finch ward, Rowan stance; Cade outside. Failed two-to-two grip costs first carry 0–2. Second: planted head, controlled foot and two downs yield 3–2. Third: opponent copies planted head; Seven rotates foot, forces shut, downs captain, transfers with elbows; final 7–2 includes down plus three over. No breathless sports commentary. The bandaged male catcher is distinct from the female captain and Kiva. Keep the north-side tray lift and two halves clear; return to base narrator."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 433,
      "title": "Friday’s draw",
      "direction": "Seven wins 7–2. Next Ropewalk first, Carrow single edge and Treen calling; Lyle has stance. Anticipation remains curiosity rather than a revenge announcement."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 463,
      "title": "The kept coin",
      "direction": "Evening quarter to seven, left fingers read ring lightly, right pain excluded. Log yes, crossing kept without request; choice feels saved rather than shut. Noa’s first returns are invitation; do not disclose later findings."
    }
  ],
